{
 "headline": "Seabrook Town’s Late Surge Secures Comeback Victory",
 "article": "Seabrook Town demonstrated tactical adaptability by switching to a higher press and more direct play after falling behind, which intensified their attacking threat and allowed for rapid counter transitions leading to four goals from 53' onwards [#1361] [#1104] [#1448]. Kian Romano’s two late goals, one from a swift counter and another following intricate build-up, effectively exploited turnovers and finished with high-quality chances, sealing the comeback win for Seabrook Town [#1882] [#1906]. Harbour City’s patient passing style yielded two goals, including Marek Barros’ long-range corner strike and Okafor’s patient build-up finish, but a red card to Joon Whitfield at 43' weakened their defensive solidity during Seabrook’s resurgence [#905] [#975] [#870]. Despite Barros’ exceptional all-round performance (1 goal, 2 assists, 9 interceptions), the team failed to contain Seabrook’s increased pressure in the second half. A key coaching point is to prepare the team to better handle high-pressure, direct attacking phases following a sending-off to avoid defensive overloads in crucial moments.",
